+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "toolChoice: 'required',",
+  "cause": "The refundAgent is configured with toolChoice 'required', which maps to Gemini's ANY mode, so after approveRefund returns a decline the model must keep making tool calls and can never send the final text reply, so it re-requests approval or loops until maxTurns is exhausted.",
+  "evidence": "Reproducing the flow against the real model with the original code: the customer message interrupts on approveRefund, and declining it makes the agent throw 'AgentError: ABORTED: Exceeded maximum tool call iterations (6)'. The Google GenAI converter maps 'required' to FunctionCallingMode.ANY (node_modules/@genkit-ai/google-genai/src/common/converters.ts:368-371). After changing it to 'auto' (matching triage), the same decline ends with finishReason 'stop' and the reply \"your refund for order A-1001 was not approved because of a duplicate claim\", repeated on a second run."
+}
